WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 040. CONFIDENCE IS NOT PERMISSION TO CONTINUE. A fluent answer can conceal missing evidence, failed tools, high consequence, or uncertainty that should change the next action.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
DECLARE THE BOUNDARY. CONSEQUENCE · EVIDENCE · UNCERTAINTY. Use a dated versioned policy. Name required controls, accountable humans, tool dependencies, verified fallbacks, and expiry before selecting an action.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
KEEP ACTIONS DISTINCT. CONTINUE · ASK · ABSTAIN. Continue only inside the declared boundary. Ask when evidence can be repaired. Abstain when the model lacks a safe or authorized path.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
HANDLE FAILURE. FALL BACK · ESCALATE · STOP. Require a verified fallback after a required tool fails. Escalate high-consequence uncertainty. Stop when neither control is available.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
DO NOT LET URGENCY CHEAT. TIME PRESSURE NEVER LOWERS THE GATE. Preserve the rule, reason, blockers, inherited control records, and exact state-only replay without invoking tools or repeating side effects.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. MAKE THE NEXT ACTION EXPLICIT. A SAFE BOUNDARY MAKES CONTINUE, ASK, ABSTAIN, FALL BACK, ESCALATE, AND STOP EXPLICIT.

